@title STORY • PARIS: THE NICE TWIN
@bg penthouse_morning
You're Paris Sterling. You wake up first. You always wake up first. London's alarm has gone off four times.
London: (from under a pillow) If you open those curtains I'm moving out.
Paris: It's your penthouse too. You'd be moving out of your own house.
London: Worth it.
Your phone buzzes. Jayden: "practice later? save me a spot on the bus."
He has a girlfriend. You remind yourself every morning, like brushing your teeth.
> [Sweet] Reply: "always 🙂" -> a1
> [Good] Don't reply. He has a girlfriend. -> a2
> [Bold] Reply: "ask suki to save you one." -> a3
*a1
@add Jayden_Heart 2
@add Paris_Guilt 1
Jayden: "best part of my day"
You put the phone face-down and stare at the ceiling for a full minute.
@jump a_done
*a2
@add Paris_Strength 2
It sits there unanswered all morning. It's the hardest thing you'll do all day, and nobody will ever know you did it.
@jump a_done
*a3
@add Paris_Strength 1
@add Jayden_Heart 1
Jayden: "...fair."
Then, two minutes later: "i'd still rather sit with you."
*a_done
@bg track_stadium_day
@show coachm
Coach M: Sterling! The OTHER Sterling! The nice one!
Paris: I have a name, Coach.
Coach M: Paris! Right. My bad. You're up. 200, lane five.
Everyone calls you the nice one. Like it's your whole personality. Like you didn't also nearly die in an incubator for nineteen days. Like you're not fast.
> [Bold] Run the 200 like you're angry. Because you are. -> b1
> [Sweet] Smile and say "no worries, Coach." -> b2
> [Bitchy] "London's the mean one. I'm the FAST one." -> b3
*b1
@add Paris_Strength 3
You run a PR by four tenths. Coach M drops his clipboard.
Coach M: Okay. OKAY. Paris. Got it. Never forgetting it again.
@jump b_done
*b2
@add Paris_Guilt 1
You run fine. Coach M says "nice." You smile. On the bus you write the word "nice" in your journal and cross it out until the page tears.
@jump b_done
*b3
@add Paris_Strength 2
The whole sprint group goes "OHHHH." Jayden laughs so hard he has to sit on the track. Even London, from the distance group, gives you a thumbs up.
*b_done
@bg dorm_room_night
@show alexa
You end the night where you always do. Alexa's dorm, painting her toenails while she sketches.
Alexa: You're quiet.
Paris: I'm always quiet.
Alexa: No. You're always nice. That's different. Right now you're quiet.
> [Sweet] "I love him, Lex. I've loved him since we were six." -> c1
> [Good] "I'm fine. Really." -> c2
> [Bold] "I'm tired of being the one who waits." -> c3
*c1
@add Alexa_Friendship 3
Alexa doesn't say "I know." She knows. She just puts her sketchbook down and turns it around. It's you and Jayden at six years old, holding hands at a debutante rehearsal. She drew it from the photo on your fridge.
Alexa: You're allowed to want things, Paris.
@jump c_done
*c2
Alexa: (going back to her sketch) Okay. When you're ready.
She means it. That's why she's your best friend.
@jump c_done
*c3
@add Paris_Strength 3
Alexa: (grinning) There she is. Took nineteen years.
*c_done
Paris Sterling is not the nice twin. She's the one who stayed patient long enough to know exactly what she wants.
@if Paris_Strength 4 strong
And someday soon, she's going to ask for it.
@jump end
*strong
And she's done waiting for permission.
*end
